    "summary": "NOAA's Nov 12 update keeps an El Niño Advisory in place: El Niño is still strengthening, with a strong-to-very strong event likely through January-March 2027. NOAA's winter outlook gives the Pacific Northwest, Mt. Hood included, some of the best odds in the country for a warmer-than-normal winter. Strong El Niño winters usually mean less Northwest snow and higher snow levels, so early-season and low-elevation skiing is the bigger risk. A Nov 18 forecast for Meadows shows only light to moderate new snow over the next several days.",
